{
	title: 'Slash commands as files',
	description: "Every slash command is one file in src/host/commands/, named like the command (cd.ts, help.ts, close.ts), found by listing the directory, so adding a command touches nothing else. Contract and rules in tasks/w4/forms.md (Commands): description, category, optional help(args), complete(args) and run(args, answers). Commands run on the host, and completion is a protocol request, so /cd ~/projec<Tab> completes against the host's files for terminal, web and remote clients alike. A command asks by returning a question (a durable form); the answer re-runs it with answers, so nothing waits in memory. Ship /help (grouped by category, /help <name> for detail) and /cd (with 'not found, create? (Y/n)'). A typed command is recorded with who typed it (see Provenance).",
	status: 'planned',
	needs: ['w4']
}
